Fix three critical bugs in SkillTreeLab.svelte:

## Bug 1: Nodes flicker and jump on hover
The CSS `.node-group:hover { transform: scale(1.15) }` OVERRIDES the inline `transform="translate(x, y)"` attribute set by Svelte. This makes nodes jump to (0,0) on hover.

FIX: Remove the CSS hover transform entirely. Instead, handle hover scaling in the Svelte template by wrapping the node content in a nested `<g>` that does the scaling. Change the node-group `<g>` to ONLY have the translate, and add an inner `<g class="node-inner">` that gets the hover scale:

```svelte
<g transform="translate({pos.x}, {pos.y})" ...handlers...>
  <g class="node-inner">
    <!-- hit area, glow, circle, text all go here -->
  </g>
</g>
```

Then the CSS becomes:
```css
.node-inner {
  transition: transform 0.15s ease-out;
  transform-origin: 0 0;
}
.node-group:hover .node-inner {
  transform: scale(1.15);
}
```

## Bug 2: Can't click on nodes — panning eats clicks
The mousedown handler on the container div triggers panning even when clicking on nodes. The event bubbles up from the node click.

FIX: In `handleMouseDown`, also check that the click target is NOT inside a `.node-group`. Add `e.target.closest('.node-group')` check:

```js
function handleMouseDown(e) {
  // Don't start panning if clicking on a node
  if (e.target.closest && e.target.closest('.node-group')) return;
  isPanning = true;
  panStart = { x: e.clientX, y: e.clientY };
}
```

Also add `e.stopPropagation()` in `handleNodeClick` to prevent it from reaching the container.

## Bug 3: Only 8 nodes visible — need more points
Change default `playerLevel` from 1 to 20 and `floorsCleared` from 0 to 10 so the user starts with 30 points and can immediately explore the tree. This is a workbench/testing tool — having enough points to play with is essential.

Apply all three fixes. Do not change anything else.
